  "issue": {
    "body": "Given a class created with a metaclass while also inheriting from Exception, https://github.com/encode/starlette/blob/master/starlette/_exception_handler.py#L17 does not properly consider this as an exception and therefore fails the below code:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nclass MyMeta(type):\r\n    def __new__(cls, name, bases, dct):\r\n        return super().__new__(cls, name, bases, dct)\r\n\r\nclass MyOutputParent(metaclass=MyMeta):\r\n    ...\r\n\r\nclass MyExceptionParent(MyOutputParent, Exception):\r\n    ...\r\n\r\nprint(f'{(Exception in type(MyExceptionParent).__mro__)=}')  # Fails (this is what the exception middleware does)\r\nprint(f'{(Exception in MyExceptionParent.__mro__)=}')  # passes\r\nprint(f'{isinstance(MyExceptionParent(), Exception)=}')  # passes\r\nprint(f'{issubclass(MyExceptionParent, Exception)=}')  # passes\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis prevents custom serialization frameworks that deal with both exceptions and metaclasses from using the built-in `app.add_exception_handler` effectively.\r\n\r\nFound on 0.23 however still present on master\n\n<!-- POLAR PLEDGE BADGE START -->\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> - We're using [Polar.sh](https://polar.sh/encode) so you can upvote and help fund this issue.\n> - We receive the funding once the issue is completed & confirmed by you.\n> - Thank you in advance for helping prioritize & fund our backlog.\n\n<a href=\"https://polar.sh/encode/starlette/issues/2273\">\n<picture>\n  <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://polar.sh/api/github/encode/starlette/issues/2273/pledge.svg?darkmode=1\">\n  <img alt=\"Fund with Polar\" src=\"https://polar.sh/api/github/encode/starlette/issues/2273/pledge.svg\">\n</picture>\n</a>\n<!-- POLAR PLEDGE BADGE END -->\n",
    "closed_at": "2023-09-12T14:23:21Z",
    "created_at": "2023-09-05T23:44:40Z",
